 "reading": "every arm returned WHOLE_SYSTEM_SYNCHRONY_FAIL with propagation also failing. Across a tenfold range of g the synchrony CV moved by 0.04 and the burst period did not move at all. This is the first row of the reviewer's outcome table: long-range coupling is exonerated as the cause of the global burst",
 "no_arm_selected": "no g is proposed as correct. The bracket was run to locate a regime transition and found none within it; selecting a value is not warranted by this evidence",
 "driver_defect": "scripts/whole_system_authority_arm.py shadows its own g parameter at lines 328 and 385 with a loop variable, so the final summary print raises TypeError after the result file is written. Every use of the real g precedes line 217, which the recorded g, arm tag and acceptance values confirm. The defect is confined to reporting and no computed value is affected; it was not repaired mid-bracket so that the four arms would differ only in g"
}
